# Plan completion — commit and release handoff

Use this checklist **after** implementation matches the plan’s acceptance criteria and you are ready to land work (not mid-flight refactors).

## Cleanup (minimal, high signal)

- Remove **dead code** and duplicate paths introduced only for experiments; prefer one source of truth (e.g. server snapshot vs parallel client delta parsing).
- Do **not** commit secrets: `backend/.env`, `frontend/.env.local`, and similar are gitignored — sync **`backend/.env.example`** (and documented frontend env vars) only when adding new knobs.
- Do **not** commit `frontend/out/` (build artifact for the wheel); ensure `npm run build` ran locally before packaging if you touch `frontend/`.
- Drop **scratch** scripts, temporary logging, and one-off probes before commit.

## Verification (scoped)

- **Backend:** `uv run pytest` on tests covering touched modules (or full suite if change is broad).
- **Frontend:** `npm run build` in `frontend/` when any dashboard/UI or env contract changed.
- **Lint:** fix new diagnostics in edited files.

## Release (`lumonox` on PyPI)

- Bump **`backend/pyproject.toml`** `version` when shipping the API wheel; workflow uploads only when the version is new on PyPI (see `.github/workflows/publish-lumonox-pypi.yml`).
- Add a one-line row to **`docs/ops/PYPI_PUBLISHING.md`** “Recent `lumonox` wheel notes” for user-visible behavior (changelog-lite). Governed spec changes still follow **`docs/DOCUMENTATION_GOVERNANCE.md`**.

## Docs touchpoints (blocking before final commit)

- **Delete** completed one-off implementation plans under `docs/` (for example `docs/*_PLAN.md`, rollout sketches, task-only writeups) once the work is merged into code and tests — do **not** keep them as stale “history” in-repo; git history already preserves the old text if needed.
- If something from a deleted plan is still **operationally** required (env vars, multi-instance behavior), fold that into **`backend/.env.example`**, **`docs/ops/*`**, or **`DEVELOPMENT.md`** only where it is canonical — avoid duplicating MVP product spec. Governed doc edits still follow **`docs/DOCUMENTATION_GOVERNANCE.md`**.

## Commit discipline

- One **logical** commit message (or follow `agents/review.md` / user request to split PRs).
- Stage only intended paths; review `git diff --staged` for accidental binaries or local exports.

## Rule self-review

When this rule materially guided the task, follow **Rules self-review** in `lumonox-execution.mdc` and apply it to this file.
